Part 1: What is the cron command and how to set it up?
What is it?
cron is a time-based job scheduler in Linux/Unix operating systems.

The line:

Bash

*/15 * * * * cd /path/to/ilims && /path/to/venv/bin/python manage.py run_reminders >> /path/to/logs/cron.log 2>&1
tells the server:

*/15 * * * *: Every 15 minutes, every hour, every day.
cd /path/to/ilims: Navigate into the project folder.
python manage.py run_reminders: Execute your reminder engine command (check for due samples, push notifications, create reminders).
>> /path/to/logs/cron.log 2>&1: Append all output or errors into a log file.
How to set it up?
Option A: On Windows (Your Development Machine C:\illms-main\)
On Windows, you have two choices:

Manual / Terminal Testing (Easiest in development):
Simply run this whenever you want to trigger the reminder engine:

cmd

python manage.py run_reminders
Windows Task Scheduler (Automatic background execution):

Press Win + R, type taskschd.msc, and hit Enter.
Click Create Basic Task...
Name it: ILIMS Reminder Engine
Trigger: Select Daily 
→
→ check Repeat task every: 15 minutes.
Action: Select Start a Program.
Program/script: C:\illms-main\venv\Scripts\python.exe
Add arguments: manage.py run_reminders
Start in: C:\illms-main
Click Finish.
Option B: On Linux (Production Deployment)
When you deploy to an Ubuntu/Debian server:

Open the crontab editor:
Bash

crontab -e
Paste the line at the bottom (replace paths with your server's actual paths):
Bash

*/15 * * * * cd /var/www/ilims && /var/www/ilims/venv/bin/python manage.py run_reminders >> /var/www/ilims/logs/cron.log 2>&1
Save and exit (Ctrl + X 
→
→ Y 
→
→ Enter).


